orname{cos}⁡(8x-ϕ),\n$$\n\nwe get the following identity:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)=(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)\n$$\n\nEquating the coefficients of $\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)$ and $\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x),$ we get the following system of equations:\n\n$$\n{\\begin{aligned}R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ=1 \\\\ R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nDividing the second equation by the first, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ}{R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ} & =1 \\\\ \\operatorname{tan}⁡ϕ & =1 \\\\ ϕ & =\\operatorname{arctan}⁡(1) \\\\ ϕ & =\\frac{\\pi }{4}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the amplitude $R.$ Squaring the first and the second equations of the system and adding the results together, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{(R\\operatorname{sin}⁡ϕ)}^{2}+{(R\\operatorname{cos}⁡ϕ)}^{2} & ={1}^{2}+{1}^{2} \\\\ {R}^{2}({sin}^{2}⁡ϕ+{cos}^{2}⁡ϕ) & =2 \\\\ {R}^{2} & =2 \\\\ R & =\\sqrt{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that we only consider the positive root since $R>0.$\n\nFinally, we can write the initial expression in amplitude-phase form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x)+\\operatorname{sin}⁡(8x)=\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})\n$$" 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291631 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291632 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291633 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291634 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1000 #edb/ref 17592186291635 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1041 "selection" 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1104 #edb/ref 17592186291631 13194139534489 true] [17592186291630 1110 #uuid "7119c7f7-91a1-5980-92f5-9960ac6b2ccf" 13194139534489 true] [17592186291631 1034 "\\sqrt{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(8x-\\frac{\\pi }{4})" 131941395